Give each LocalStore its own temporary roots file.

LocalStore names the file <stateDir>/temproots/<pid>, and its comment
says why that is safe: a file with this process's pid "*must* be stale,
since there can be no two processes with the same pid" (gc.cc:57). A
second LocalStore on the same state directory in the same process breaks
that. It takes the first store's file for a stale one and deletes it, so
the collector no longer sees the first store's temporary roots and may
delete a path that store is using. When the two open the file at the
same moment, the second one waits in flock for ever instead.

`nix` opens one store per process. An embedder such as huggorm opens as
many as its callers ask for. nanopynix's
test_two_handles_on_one_local_store_keep_each_others_temp_roots drives
the deletion. Later Nix git gives each store its own name with
makeTempPath; the 2.36pre that nixpkgs carries does not yet, so drop
this patch once the bound Nix does.

The file is <pid>-<n> now, with n counted per process. findTempRoots
reads the pid with std::stoi, which stops at the '-', so every Nix that
reads the directory still reads the name.

--- a/src/libstore/local-store.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/local-store.cc
@@ -50,6 +50,8 @@

 #include <nlohmann/json.hpp>

+#include <atomic>
+
 #include "nix/util/strings.hh"

 #include "store-config-private.hh"
@@ -114,6 +116,12 @@
     SQLiteStmt QueryValidPaths;
 };

+/* One temporary roots file per LocalStore, not per process: a second
+   store in this process would otherwise take the first one's file for a
+   stale one and delete it. findTempRoots reads the pid with stoi, which
+   stops at the '-'. */
+static std::atomic<uint64_t> nextTempRootsFile{0};
+
 LocalStore::LocalStore(ref<const Config> config)
     : Store{*config}
     , LocalFSStore{*config}
@@ -124,7 +132,7 @@
     , reservedPath(dbDir / "reserved")
     , schemaPath(dbDir / "schema")
     , tempRootsDir(config->stateDir.get() / "temproots")
-    , fnTempRoots(tempRootsDir / std::to_string(getpid()))
+    , fnTempRoots(tempRootsDir / (std::to_string(getpid()) + "-" + std::to_string(nextTempRootsFile++)))
 {
     auto state(_state->lock());
     state->stmts = std::make_unique<State::Stmts>();
